<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan aluminium output down 2 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan aluminium output down 2 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian January primary aluminium output fell two percent from December 1996 and rose two percent from January 1996 levels, State Statistics Committee data showed on Friday. The committee gave no outright production figures.</p>
<p>It issued the following data for January metals production in percentage changes --</p>
<p>	     RUSSIAN METALS OUTPUT IN JANUARY 1997</p>
<p>			(PERCENTAGE CHANGES)</p>
<p>			  Jan 1997 as pct  Jan 1997 as pct</p>
<p>			     of Dec 1996	  of Jan 1996</p>
<p>Primary aluminium	    98		  102</p>
<p>Alumina			 112		   94</p>
<p>Bauxite			  46		   69</p>
<p>Copper (refined)	     89		  106</p>
<p>Copper (concentrates)	72		   79</p>
<p>Nickel			   93		   97</p>
<p>Cobalt			  106		  125</p>
<p>Gold (mined)		   59		  148</p>
<p>Titanium sponge	     101		  163</p>
<p>--Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
